  "source_attribution": "The s 102 difference image is concentrated at the target; its positive-deficit centroid offset is 0.139 pixel, descriptive only. The 60 arcsec Gaia census contains 71 sources. Two non-target sources remain capable under optimistic G-band full-capture assumptions at the minimum measured 25.312 ppt aperture loss: Gaia 6070540006339062784 at 8.588 arcsec (about 0.409 TESS pixel), requiring 18.85% intrinsic loss, and Gaia 6070539967673962240 at 41.794 arcsec (about 1.990 pixel), requiring 15.77%. The close neighbor cannot be cleanly separated by this broad pixel deficit. A target-like peak alone does not exclude that neighbor. Source attribution remains unresolved.",
  "independent_reduction": "An independent custom TESScut extraction of the s 102 event at BTJD 4128.98299 reproduces the loss: central 1 x 1,3 x 3,5 x 5 apertures give 40.384,40.446,25.312 ppt. The alternative reduction is deliberately compared by its own diluted depth, not forced to the 51.875 ppt QLP median.",
  "limitations": "The event is real and repeats, but a capable 8.59 arcsec Gaia neighbor prevents definitive target ownership. Aperture dilution varies strongly, and TIC 241479387 has mild roughly 2 sigma Gaia period/conjunction tension. Timing fit errors are conditional and exclude extraction/model systematics. No exhaustive all-sector characterization or Monte Carlo was performed. Novelty remains pending because scoped catalogue coverage is incomplete.",
  "next_check": "Obtain resolved eclipse photometry separating the 8.59 arcsec neighbor, and compare a new timed eclipse or velocities with the Gaia orbit.",
